      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_5cd40ee71ccbbc161661c0917de47df069678ee269cf3362234aa7156cda9a43",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Phase-amplitude separation isolates exponential growth from prefactors, while frequency decomposition converts oscillation into a parameter shift of the phase. The hard asymptotic question is thereby reduced to locating and comparing finitely many admissible critical points.",
