    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4da6895365766e7617058c0c392f507c1cb170a5abce385ab8a4f3d0b5a678ea",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The construction has three rate budgets with different roles: prime-adic common-divisor saving reduces normalization cost, saddle geometry controls exponential smallness of the linear form, and a distinct coefficient estimate controls the size of its rational coefficients. Finite-panel irrationality follows when the first two budgets satisfy the source's strict negativity condition, while the dimension bound additionally compares coefficient growth; parameter choices tune these budgets together with the supported zeta range.",
