      "proposed_content": "The source uses related algebraic saddle data for two different asymptotic tasks: frequency-indexed saddles and their contour geometry determine the exponential size of the linear form, while auxiliary horizontal integrals select a minimal-modulus imaginary root to sharpen the exponential bound on its coefficients. Their eventual comparison therefore measures usefulness against representation cost rather than duplicating one asymptotic estimate.",
